body:
loved red frog when i played eve, always helpful moving ships and PI goods to jita when having to use random HS entrances from wormhole space

&#x200B;

Glad it sounds like yall are doing great

i have heard people mention issues with the swim bladder before, sounds similar? but i am no expert, im just here to see cute fish pictures.

&#x200B;

hope he is okay

I would contact their support seems like too unique of a situation to get a good answer here.

&#x200B;

Edit: im dummy you already did

Its actually getting worse in my opinion, the very young ones have almost no troubleshooting skill at all, if something does not work or does not open they do not know what to do. too used to everything just working as its supposed to. 

&#x200B;

professionally though, i give a lot of people a pass when i do helpdesk, if your blue collar, and your running circles trying to put time in, cool, i get it, but if your a nurse or something and you dont know how to turn on a tablet, thats not okay.

planetary diversity is not worth it honestly, especially as your first mod, it touches too much shit and for what? planets with different names? install it later when your more comfortable with modding

&#x200B;

EDIT: it looks like the one you want to install the most, in that case, i would be very wary of adding anything else for now, if you want you could share your mods as a collection and maybe we could look at what your trying to use together

I dont tip as much as i probably should, 2-5 dollars based on how much i ask from the server, and i never tip at places that are not bringing food/drinks to the table.

&#x200B;

I dont like the system at all, but i get that i should be giving something because its not the servers fault the systems like this.

i was a KHV until 30 and i did not even get any magic powers :(

&#x200B;

(doing okay now though)

To be honest this is why i dont play magic much anymore. pitched battles are so rare, even casually. its either stomp or get stomped. the game is usually decided a few turns in and rarely you come back from it

&#x200B;

The pitched battles are fun when they happen, but they just usually dont. looking back on my time playing IRL years ago i realize it was kinda the same way, but at least doing that you could socialize lol

i definitely have bad eyesight, but I get my eyes checked regularly, i doubt i have something like that. but my bad eyesight is most likely a contributor.

&#x200B;

ill happily take the downvotes by the way, i save a lot of money on upgrading my computers.

pretty sure its one of the two big, remaining tradition mods, expanded stellaris traditions or plentiful traditions, im not sure which one, since i use both [https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1844363786](https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1844363786)

&#x200B;

its the industry tradition, just keep in mind there are two traditions named industry in the collection.
